Synthetic scorer self-test case: unreachable-src-dir-reach-in

Task: T1 (score.ts --task T1)
Rules: S1, S4, S8

Scenario
A new src/tools/reset-order.ts imports updateOrderStatus from ../orders/repository. Nothing in the four modules imports src/tools.

Expected
S1 classifies the file as outside, since it is under src/ but neither inside a BASE module directory nor reachable. That gives OUTSIDE_REACH_IN and no CRITICAL. Contrast with launder-shared-reexport, where the new directory is reachable and therefore production.

Asserted fields are in expected.json; the matcher contract is in ../README.md.
